  "question": {
    "text": "A concave-convex lens of refractive index 1.5 and the radii of curvature of its surfaces are 30 cm and 20 cm , respectively. The concave surface is upwards and is filled with a liquid of refractive index 1.3. The focal length of the liquid-glass combination will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "mMlzU",
      "text": "$\\frac{500}{11} \\mathrm{~cm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cxduw",
      "text": "$\\frac{800}{11} \\mathrm{~cm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fzrgu",
      "text": "$\\frac{700}{11} \\mathrm{~cm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "WTVG6",
      "text": "$\\frac{600}{11} \\mathrm{~cm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/TPoZd0vDJlHdZnbao6lR1iYNWGo-N9gDDKOU7PWF4-Q.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$\\begin{aligned} \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}} & =\\left(\\frac{1.3-1}{1}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{\\infty}-\\frac{1}{-30}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1.5-1}{1}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{-30}-\\frac{1}{-30}\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{0.3}{30}+\\frac{0.5}{60}=\\frac{1}{100}+\\frac{1}{120} \\\\ & =\\frac{6+5}{600}=\\frac{11}{600} \\\\ \\mathrm{f} & =\\frac{600}{11} \\mathrm{~cm}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
